items/ex-one-point-compactifications-of-the-line-and-of-the-naturals.md:109:**Where compactness does the work for the circle.** Producing the inverse of $h$ explicitly is possible here and was done at step 2.3, but continuity of that inverse is never checked: [L7] supplies it from compactness of $\mathbb{R}^{*}$ and the Hausdorff property of $S^1$. That is the standard use of claim 3 of [[thm-compactness-under-continuous-maps]].
