\\in \\mathbb{N}$\nwith $|x_k - x_l| < \\varepsilon$ for all $k, l \\ge K$. This page builds the\ntoolkit for those two notions and does not restate them. A sequence\n**converges** if it converges to some real, and **diverges** if it does not.",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-apply.log:6778:      "quote": "Every complete ordered field $F$ ([[def-complete-ordered-field]]) is Archimedean:\nfor every $x \\in F$ there is a natural number $n \\ge 1$ with $x < n \\cdot 1_F$,\nwhere $n \\cdot 1_F$ is the canonical natural of the ordered field $F$\n([[def-ordered-field]]). Equivalently, the canonical naturals are cofinal in $F$.",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-apply.log:6787:      "quote": "Let $F$ be an ordered field, with field structure as in [[def-field]], and for\n$n \\ge 1$ let $n \\cdot 1_F$ denote the canonical natural number\n$\\underbrace{1_F + \\cdots + 1_F}_{n}$, defined recursively by $1 \\cdot 1_F = 1_F$\nand $(n+1) \\cdot 1_F = n \\cdot 1_F + 1_F$. Then for every $n \\ge 1$:\n\n- $n \\cdot 1_F > 0$ and $(n+1) \\cdot 1_F > n \\cdot 1_F$;\n- the map $n \\mapsto n \\cdot 1_F$ is strictly increasing, hence injective, on $\\{1, 2, 3, \\dots\\}$;\n- $(m+n) \\cdot 1_F = m \\cdot 1_F + n \\cdot 1_F$ and $(mn) \\cdot 1_F = (m \\cdot 1_F)(n \\cdot 1_F)$ for all $m, n \\ge 1$.",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-apply.log:6797:      "quote": "Let $F$ be an ordered field ([[def-ordered-field]]) with positive cone $P$, and\nlet $a, b \\in F$.\n\n1. If $a > 0$ then $a^{-1} > 0$.\n2. If $0 < a < b$ then $0 < b^{-1} < a^{-1}$.",
