research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f6-examples.log:6546:DEFECT: The cited definitions construct the reals, define their order, and define what a complete ordered field is; they do not prove that the constructed reals are totally ordered or complete. Thus the premise needed to invoke the Archimedean theorem is unsupported, as is the totality used in step 1.3.  
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f6-examples.log:6547:EVIDENCE: The cited def-real-numbers Definition says only that the reals are the quotient ring of Cauchy sequences by null sequences. The missing on-disk results are thm-reals-ordered-field, titled “The reals form a totally ordered field”, and cor-cauchy-reals-lub-complete, titled “The Cauchy-sequence reals have the least-upper-bound property”.  
