research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-alpha-a6.log:32:I also read the round-3 repair against its targets myself. [L3] now says ℝ is a totally ordered field with the least-upper-bound property, hence a complete ordered field; `thm-reals-ordered-field` states "makes $\mathbb{R}$ a totally ordered field" and `cor-cauchy-reals-lub-complete` states the least-upper-bound property and the complete-ordered-field conclusion verbatim. Both are in `deps`. My reading is that it is exact — but my reading is not the certification, which is the point of the lane.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-t2-compactness-theorems.log:10:DEFECT: Neither cited definition states that the defined order makes the reals a totally ordered field. The first merely defines the relation and delegates trichotomy to another theorem; the second defines completeness for a field already assumed to be ordered. Thus L8 is not licensed by its citations.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-t2-compactness-theorems.log:12:EVIDENCE: The cited `def-real-order` says, "Independence of the representative, trichotomy, and compatibility with the field operations: [[thm-reals-ordered-field]]." The cited `def-complete-ordered-field` begins, "Let $F$ be an ordered field," and then defines when such a field is complete. The actual Statement of `thm-reals-ordered-field` is: "The relation of [[def-real-order]] is well defined and makes $\mathbb{R}$ ([[thm-reals-field]]) a totally ordered field."
