research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-t2-compactness-theorems.result.json:16:  "tail": "### FINDING 1 — thm-compactness-under-continuous-maps — L8 cites definitions that do not establish the real-order properties used\n\nLOCATION: Facts & Assumptions, line 86; used in proof steps 5.2 and 6.1\n\nQUOTE: \"[L8] The order of $\\mathbb{R}$ is a total order: no real satisfies $s < s$, and $s < t$ together with $t \\le s$ is impossible ([[def-real-order]], [[def-complete-ordered-field]]).\"\n\nDEFECT: Neither cited definition states that the defined order makes the reals a totally ordered field. The first merely defines the relation and delegates trichotomy to another theorem; the second defines completeness for a field already assumed to be ordered. Thus L8 is not licensed by its citations.\n\nEVIDENCE: The cited `def-real-order` says, \"Independence of the representative, trichotomy, and compatibility with the field operations: [[thm-reals-ordered-field]].\" The cited `def-complete-ordered-field` begins, \"Let $F$ be an ordered field,\" and then defines when such a field is complete. The actual Statement of `thm-reals-ordered-field` is: \"The relation of [[def-real-order]] is well defined and makes $\\mathbb{R}$ ([[thm-reals-field]]) a totally ordered field.\"\n\nSEVERITY: fatal\n\nMINIMAL REPAIR: In `deps`, replace `def-complete-ordered-field` with `thm-reals-ordered-field`; in L8 cite `thm-reals-ordered-field` for the total-order assertion.\n\n## Coverage\nItems read in full: thm-compact-iff-fip, thm-closed-subspace-of-a-compact-space-is-compact, thm-compact-subset-of-a-hausdorff-space-is-closed, thm-compactness-under-continuous-maps, thm-compactness-agrees-with-metric-compactness\nItems not read, and why: none\nFacts checked against their target on disk: 28\nFindings: 1 fatal, 0 nonfatal"
