\mathbb{N}$\nwith $|x_k - x_l| < \\varepsilon$ for all $k, l \\ge K$. This page builds the\ntoolkit for those two notions and does not restate them. A sequence\n**converges** if it converges to some real, and **diverges** if it does not.",
