    39	## Remarks
    40	
    41	- Two Cauchy sequences define the same real exactly when their difference is a
    42	  null sequence.
    43	- That $\mathbb{R}$ is a field is [[thm-reals-field]]; its order is
    44	  [[def-real-order]].
    35	
    36	The relation of [[def-real-order]] is well defined and makes $\mathbb{R}$
    37	([[thm-reals-field]]) a totally ordered field.
